>
  <h2>Whatever your idea, we will make it a reality</h2>
  <p>
    Here at CPF, we specialize in custom stonework and stonemasonry features for
    your home or commercial space. We also offer design and conceptual drawings
    for your upcoming projects. Below you will find some of our recent custom
    stonework in Thousand Oaks, Newbury Park and Agoura Hills.
  </p>

  <h2>Rubble masonry and ashlar masonry</h2>
  <p>
    Custom stonework, also known as stonemasonry, has been around since the
    human race first began using tools. Stonework can be divided into two main
    category types: <strong>rubble masonry</strong> and <strong>ashlar
    masonry</strong>. Rubble masonry is the art of using roughly dressed stones
    and mortar, whereas ashlar masonry is that of using cut — neatly dressed —
    stones and mortar to build features.
  </p>
  <p>
    Some of the features you will commonly find are stone walkways, retaining
    walls, garden walls and stone veneer. Stone veneer is a beautiful
    alternative to traditional siding on a home: it can drastically improve the
    home's aesthetic character for a reasonably low investment of time and
    money.
  </p>
  <p>
    We at CPF have hundreds of jobs under our belts for each type of stonework.
    Pat Flaherty, founder of CPF Masonry, has been driving stonemasonry projects
    of all sizes from concept to completion in Southern California since 1991,
    and is your go-to resource for your next project.
  </p>

  <h3>Where stone meets everything else</h3>
  <p>
    Very little stonework stands on its own. A stone-faced retaining wall is
    holding back real earth and needs the footing and drainage of a
    <a href={withBase('/masonry/')}>structural wall</a>; sidewalk and driveway
    features get poured with the
    <a href={withBase('/custom-concrete/')}>concrete work</a>. The
    <a href={withBase('/featured-project-dos-vientos-villa/')}>Dos Vientos Villa</a>
    project is most of this page in one address.
  </p>

  <h2>Owner supervised, fully insured</h2>
  <p>
    Stonework is judged at arm's length for the life of the house — the joints
    and the stone selection are the craft, and neither is recoverable after the
    mortar sets. <strong>Each project is owner supervised</strong>, and CPF is
    <strong>licensed, insured and bonded</strong> under C-29 masonry and C-8
    concrete.
  </p>
